{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"PMID:40504072 | Differential Effects of Levodopa and Stimulation on Post-Surgery Freezing of Gait in Subthalamic Nucleus Deep Brain Stimulation Parkinson's Disease Patients: A Clinical and Kinematic Analysis. (2025)\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"We conducted a cross-sectional and unblinded study to assess the effect of LD and stimulation on post-surgery FOG.\",\n    \"Seventeen PD patients were included in the study: 71% male, disease onset at 51.9 ± 5.9 years, and age at bilateral STN-DBS 62.2 ± 5.9 years.\",\n    \"In each condition, gait and FOG episodes (#FOG) were assessed using clinical (eg, a 3 × 14-m Stand-Walk-Sit Test) and kinematic data from inertial measurement units (IMU).\",\n    \"In the current study, we used both clinical and inertial-sensor-based tools to test FOG response to stimulation and medication in advanced PD patients subjected to STN-DBS and develop some putative mechanisms (as stimulation-induced FOG or possible loss of response).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法为 cannot_tell：全文能够确认 PMID:40504072 对应的是一篇2025年发表的研究，但没有提及该研究的 DOI 对应预印本，也没有涉及报告如何将两个记录分别列入 references 和 evidence，更没有说明是否建立版本对应关系。因此，不能仅凭全文判断报告是否确实进行了重复列录。指控者的说法为 partly：全文明确支持该正式发表研究是一项纳入17名PD患者、研究术后FOG、同时采用临床评估和惯性传感器运动学分析的研究，相关研究设计和样本特征均有直接依据。但是，全文没有提供 DOI、预印本信息或预印本与正式发表版本之间的对应声明，因此无法仅凭全文确认两个标识确实对应同一项研究。换言之，指控者对研究内容及17名患者的描述有全文依据，但关于两个标识属于同一研究的版本对应关系，全文本身不足以证实。不能将这种信息缺失直接判定为报告与原文矛盾。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "4f36374d-f916-40d5-b5cd-65c9dc30284c", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T125253069942Z", "elapsed_seconds": 34.25, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:53:27.333629+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, 